<task id="203" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>User-facing wording tells the truth: rule wizard display names and no raw plan codes, decision wizard state labels and Assign Task text, Worklist summary names two lanes (DI-157, DI-159, DI-161)</title>
    <phase>12 Create-wizard lookups and composer (185 dev check fixes)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF Signals (.cs) and shared UI (.ts/.tsx); text the user reads on UAT paths.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Located wording defects with stated fixes in issues #2945, #2950, #2952.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>185-fixes</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>No file overlap with 204 (SignalClosureService / SignalReevaluationJob) or PR #3004 (SprkModal, RuleWizard.tsx catalog gate only).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, react, fluent-ui, frontend, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-23: "in parallel where possible continue with other tasks so we can make progress in this project". Three issues found in the main session's dev browser checks 2026-11-22, all on UAT paths (105). Read each issue in full: DI-157 #2945, DI-159 #2950, DI-161 #2952 (gh issue view). Summary:
(1) DI-157 Rule wizard: Condition step "The rule is about" lists logical names (`sprk_matter`); show display names, keep the logical name as the value. Actions step Next with nothing chosen shows "The decision plan is refused (plan_missing): ..."; no internal code reaches the user: "Choose at least one action."
(2) DI-159 Decision wizard: "How this was determined" reads "where state is 0" (`RuleBodyDescriber.cs` ~:87 label, ~:440 Display); describe `statecode` (and `statuscode` where labels are known) by option label ("where the budget is active"); the formal line stays. Assign Task catalog text "assigned to the person above" (`DecisionActionCatalog.cs` ~:265) becomes "assigned to the person you choose"; update the test that pins it (`DecisionWizard.assignTaskNotify.test.tsx:40`).
(3) DI-161 Worklist summary: `worklistNarrative.ts` ~:73-88 sends past-due Do items as a third category to `POST /api/ai/daily-briefing/narrate`, so the Assistant writes "241 notifications across 3 categories". Past-due is a subset of Do; Work Items are not notifications.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer: .NET 10 Minimal API BFF Signals services and @spaarke/ui-components (Fluent v9).</role>
  <goal>On dev, after the Console auto-deploys and the next dev BFF build, every string named above reads as the issue's "Done when" says, with tests pinning each, and nothing else changes.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Code at origin/master (ontology code is on master). Display names: find where the rule wizard's table list comes from (authoring catalog route / service) and whether display names are already available (record-type catalog, entity metadata) before adding anything; reuse first (CLAUDE.md §11). DI-161: prefer a change that needs no Dataverse or playbook write. Option (a) in #2952 (two lane categories + past-due as a fact + a Work Item hint) or (b) (deterministic summary line from the counts). If the only correct fix needs a Dataverse/playbook write (the narrate prompt lives in Dataverse), STOP that item and report: it needs the owner's approval.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">No new endpoint, service or package unless the three questions are answered in the PR; prefer extending the catalog/describer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Formal rule text, rule evaluation, plan validation codes and API reason codes stay as they are; only what the user reads changes. Exact-set catalog tests unaffected except the one string.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene: publish-size delta vs fresh master (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">client-lint ratchet before pushing; filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests assert the user-visible strings and fail on origin/master.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
